==Trivia==
*Cannons were invented in China during the twelfth century. It was most likely developed in parallel or as an evolution of an earlier gunpowder weapon called the fire lance. Cannons were used for warfare by the late thirteenth century in the Yuan dynasty and spread throughout Eurasia in the fourteenth century. During the late Middle Ages, large and small cannons were developed for siege and field battles. The cannon replaced prior siege weapons such as the trebuchet. After the late Middle Ages, most large cannons were abandoned in favor of greater numbers of lighter, more maneuverable field artillery.
**The Royal Giant is 1 of 4 [[cards]] associated with cannonry, with the others being [[Cannon]], [[Cannon Cart]], and [[Cannoneer]].
**Oddly, the cannonball he holds is larger than the cannonball fired from his cannon. Even so, the Royal Giant can be seen loading this cannonball back into the cannon during the recoil animation after he fires.
*The Royal Giant is 1 of 20 cards associated with nobility, with the others being [[Knight]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Royal Delivery]], [[Tower Princess]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Prince]], [[Raging Prince]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Princess]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Spirit Empress]], [[Super Knight]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Royal Chef]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], and the [[Little Prince]].
**In the Spanish and Finnish language settings of the game, the Royal Giant's name translates to "Noble Giant".
*The Royal Giant is one of the first troop cards to receive a [[Card Evolution]], alongside the [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], and [[Firecracker]].
*The Royal Giant is 1 of 15 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which bring an excited reaction from the audience upon spawning and brings a collective groan from the audience when defeated, as well as a concerning gasp when the opponent plays him and applause when he's destroyed, the others include the [[Giant]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Rune Giant]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Golem]], [[Bowler]], [[Electro Wizard]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Sparky]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], [[Super Lava Hound]], and the [[Monk]].
*Despite wearing an armor, he has less hit points than an equal-level Giant. This is likely for balancing reasons.
*The cannon he wields appears to be the turret of a Level 7 Cannon in Clash of Clans. His [[Star Points|Star Level 2 skin]] has a cannon that resembles the Level 10 Cannon in Clash of Clans.
*The Royal Giant was once very infamous among players for being overpowered due to his range and high hit points, meaning that he was harder to take down before landing a highly damaging shot. This is referenced in the game a few times:
**A [[Loading Screen Hints|Loading Screen Hint]] that reads “''All cards are created equally… even Royal Giants.''”.
**A post-[[Basics of Battle|battle]] [[2v2]] message that says “''Nerf the Royal Giant''”.
*While not available as a troop in Boom Beach, the Royal Giant made an appearance in an April Fool's [https://youtu.be/Z8XT_cP7bsA?si=tzV1XUjCE7NB1jfB video] that Supercell posted in Boom Beach's Youtube channel.
*The Royal Giant is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
**He is also the only card in which an Emote has changed.
**The [https://clashroyale.fandom.com/wiki/Emotes?file=Royal_Giant_Gorgeous.png Royal Giant Gorgeous Emote] is a reference to the Royal Giant's card description.
*Despite the Damage Dealer [[Card Mastery]] task mentioning that the Royal Giant can deal damage to troops or [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]], he cannot progress the task by dealing damage to troops.
**The Royal Giant is 1 of 6 troops that cannot deal damage to other troops whatsoever, the others being the Giant, [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Elixir Golem]], and Rune Giant.
***However, the Royal Giant's Evolution changes this, as the recoil from shooting will cause him to deal area damage to any ground troop nearby.

